{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#261","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#261","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#261\",\"parent_revision\":\"9d113b25d9d94a9f20eab5239520071e5bed5e7ba3433c0a1040867a7b667c1a\",\"root_revision\":\"9d113b25d9d94a9f20eab5239520071e5bed5e7ba3433c0a1040867a7b667c1a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap the various scripts under python3-development (mkdocs sync, uv release sync) as MCP tools. Agents could manage Python project tooling without shell access. Tools: `sync_mkdocs`, `sync_uv_releases`, `check_python_environment`.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 -- Useful quality-of-life improvement enabling agents to manage Python tooling without shell access. Not blocking any current workflows. Deprioritized by the ongoing plugin redesign (python_plugin_redesign.md) which may change which scripts/skills are retained.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nBottleneck: agents must invoke toolchain scripts via Bash tool, bypassing MCP tool access control. Blocks: nothing currently.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\nAgents can trigger sync_uv_releases without shell access. Provides clean MCP interface for Python toolchain operations consistent with development-harness MCP pattern.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA PEP 723 runner script at plugins/python3-development/scripts/run_toolchain_server.py that launches a FastMCP server exposing confirmed toolchain scripts as tools. The plugin.json mcpServers key registers the server. Only confirmed working scripts are wrapped.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. fastmcp list against the toolchain server script exits 0 and lists sync_uv_releases as a tool\\\\n2. Calling sync_uv_releases via MCP server returns the same result as running the script directly\\\\n3. plugin.json mcpServers key references the runner script and server starts cleanly on plugin load\\\\n4. Each exposed tool has a docstring\\\\n5. uv run prek run against the server script exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/python3-development/skills/uv/scripts/sync_uv_releases.py -- only confirmed wrappable script |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/agentskill-kaizen/mcp/server.py -- FastMCP PEP 723 server pattern |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py -- plugin MCP runner wrapper pattern |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/python3-development/.claude-plugin/plugin.json -- where mcpServers entry must be added |\\\\n| Prior work | plugins/python3-development/python_plugin_redesign.md -- active redesign; read before building |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nDepends on: scope clarification (wrap only sync_uv_releases vs. first build missing scripts). Depends on: python3-development plugin redesign reaching stable state or explicit decision to proceed before. Blocks: None identified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall (wrapping sync_uv_releases only) or Medium (if sync_mkdocs and check_python_environment scripts must first be created). FastMCP server pattern is established. A server wrapping one confirmed script is roughly one day of focused work.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nsync_mkdocs has no backing script -- mkdocs SKILL.md is an incomplete stub. check_python_environment has no backing script anywhere in the plugin. Scope must be clarified with human before implementation begins.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail. Rationale: Toolchain scripts exist as standalone executables but lack an MCP interface; agents cannot access them without shell bypass. Analysis Method: design-framing. Scenario Target: Agent needs to sync uv releases -> invokes MCP tool instead of Bash shell command.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. Should sync_mkdocs and check_python_environment be created as new scripts before wrapping, or should the initial MCP server be limited to sync_uv_releases only?\\\\n2. item_type is Docs in GitHub -- should this be corrected to Feature?\\\\n3. Should this MCP server wait for the plugin redesign (python_plugin_redesign.md) to stabilise before implementation?\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\nAPPROVED-WITH-GAPS \u2014 sync_uv_releases script confirmed; sync_mkdocs and check_python_environment scripts do not exist and must be created or descoped before implementation.\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/python3-development/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **python3-development: python development toolchain mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2fa311e41e393b303a27a325f987deec20464c17b91d79d9bbb918eafd073691\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTBTzQ\"}"}